INT. DERELICT ORPHANAGE, WEST WING DORMITORY - NIGHT

Iron beds in rows. Mildewed mattresses. A rocking horse with one glass eye. Moonlight through a shattered window.

Three paranormal investigators move in a tight triangle, flashlights jittering.

DR. EUGENIA FALLOWFIELD-ADEYEMI (50s, parapsychologist, wool coat, an old tape recorder in her hand) leads.

NOAH "NO" OKWUOSA-BERGMAN (20s, camera operator, headlamp) films over her shoulder.

LENA TAKAHASHI-DUMONT (30s, sound engineer, headphones, boom mic) sweeps the room with a long pole.

EUGENIA
(to the group)
Quiet, please. I want a clean recording.

NOAH
Copy.

LENA
Copy.

They freeze. The tape recorder whirs. A long beat. The wind moves through the dormitory like breath.

EUGENIA
(into the recorder)
Is anyone here?

Silence. Then, faintly, from the far end:

CHILD (O.S.)
Yes.

All three jump. Lena stumbles into the rocking horse; it sways, creaking. Noah's camera light lurches.

EUGENIA
(whispering)
Did you hear that?

LENA
Yes.

NOAH
I got it.

EUGENIA
(into the recorder)
What is your name?

CHILD (O.S.)
Wren.

EUGENIA
Hello, Wren. How old are you?

CHILD (O.S.)
Nine.

EUGENIA
Do you live here?

CHILD (O.S.)
We all do.

The temperature drops. Their breath fogs.

LENA
(to herself)
Okay. Okay. This is fine.

NOAH
It's very fine.

LENA
It's extremely fine.

EUGENIA
Wren, can you show us where you are?

A pause. Then, down the dormitory aisle, a lantern flickers into being. Under it stands a small figure in a gray nightshirt, hands clasped, face pale and ordinary.

NOAH
Oh my god.

EUGENIA
(steady)
Hello, Wren.

WREN
(smiling)
Hello.

She tilts her head. Behind her, the iron beds begin to rattle, one by one.

LENA
Eugenia.

EUGENIA
I see them.

WREN
They're excited.

EUGENIA
Why?

WREN
You're the first visitors.

Eugenia opens her mouth. Closes it.

NOAH
(whispering)
Please tell me we're leaving.

EUGENIA
Not yet.

LENA
Eugenia!

EUGENIA
Not yet. Wren, who is the one at the back?

Beyond Wren, in the darkness, a tall shape unfolds from the last bed. A woman in a nurse's uniform, face hidden in shadow.

WREN
That's Matron.

LENA
(very quietly)
Matron.

WREN
She's not very nice.

The nurse steps forward. A single stride, and the whole room tilts. The beds slide. The glass in the window sings. Lena shrieks and drops the mic. Noah's camera light flares and goes out. Eugenia stumbles against an iron frame.

EUGENIA
(shouting)
Out! Everyone, out!

They run. The dormitory stretches around them, doors multiplying, corridors lengthening. Lena sobs. Noah curses. Eugenia, hand on the wall, counts doors under her breath.

EUGENIA (CONT'D)
Seven. Eight. Nine. Here!

She slams through a door. They tumble into the courtyard, grass and moonlight, cold clean air.

They lie gasping. The orphanage looms behind them, windows dark.

LENA
(weeping)
Never again.

NOAH
I lost the camera.

EUGENIA
(softly)
No. You have the tape.

She holds up the recorder, its light still green. She presses play.

Her own voice: "Is anyone here?" A pause. Then a small voice, unmistakable:

TAPE (V.O.)
Come back.

They stare at the recorder. Slowly, without a word, Lena takes it, crouches, and buries it in the dirt.
